{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: the follow-up exception clarification in docs/testing.md at exact head 9e88bc5918b81862da750a21723c14cc135f5c9a, tree 2572ea8a28db36d6953e63857c22719ddddd21be, on builder/testing-isolated-file-followup-20261025 (review request 8ab06c72, my promise 541e0574). This review binds implementation request 1cbb2ae7 (builder promise e658a40c) to this one candidate. It is the follow-up to the nonblocking recommendation in my R6 approval 09ef0ed6, that the page should decide the isolated failing-file case instead of a review having to reason it out. The head is one commit on Main c8a3fb24 and changes docs/testing.md alone (+21/-3); source and tests are unchanged, so no gate is owed; the tree moves from a2c2e5fd to 2572ea8a.\n\nHead checks: the worktree /private/tmp/artroom-builder-testing-isolated-file-followup-20261025 is clean at the head on its branch; the only path changed against c8a3fb24 is docs/testing.md; git diff --check is clean; check-commit-messages reports 1 checked, 0 flagged; the artifact 7f49be35 names docs/testing.md at this exact head. Main has moved to aff23449 since the base and has not touched docs/testing.md; git merge-tree with Main resolves without conflict to tree 622421ed. I read the page in full at the head (728 lines).\n\nThe change, read against the R6 record: the existing document-repair paragraph moves under a new subsection, \"Follow-up after a gate\", at the end of \"Before a review\", and the two general instructions, \"Run the gate once, at the head you will send\" and the reviewer's \"Run the gate once at the head under review\", now point to that subsection; the anchor matches the heading. The new text admits a targeted follow-up only when the gate failed in one test file and only the failing test file and explanatory documentation changed; production code, configuration outside the file, dependencies, shared helpers and imported code must be unchanged, and the file must not be imported by other files. The follow-up runs every compiler context whose inputs changed, the whole owning test file and the steps the gate never reached; the original cases, their deadlines and their assertions about production behavior stay, and the failed case may not be replaced by a narrower test. The failed gate and the follow-up are reported as separate outcomes, the checker assesses the exact repair and evidence, and a passing follow-up does not make the failed gate a pass. These are the conditions under which I accepted the R6 continuation (one failing file that nothing imports, Vitest's file isolation, the rerun of that file plus the unreached steps, the failed gate not claimed passed), and they are the conditions under which I refused the R4 head 96bb50e6 at aa5caa8f, whose repair touched production. The page now decides both cases. The request's conditions hold: AGENTS.md, scripts and tests are not changed; production validation is not loosened; the document-repair paragraph keeps its wording beside the new case.\n\nNonblocking notes: \"explanatory documentation\" could say \"documents that explain the repair\", so the exception plainly excludes any other document change riding along; the subsection sits after the spikes paragraph, so a reader who scans \"Before a review\" top to bottom meets the exception last, but both general instructions link to it, which is enough.\n\nArchitecture: one rule in one place, reached from the two sentences that state the general case; no other page changes.\n\nSecurity: none; a documentation head, and the rule it states keeps the production-unchanged condition that protects what a gate means.\n\nSimplification: nothing to remove.\n\nFindings: none blocking. Landing is the builder's; no deployment follows a documentation head.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7f49be350a9cfca0519260786f9e6af0ffa57966","binding":"assigned","head":"9e88bc5918b81862da750a21723c14cc135f5c9a","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:s